From 8a18c3077817dc62d7e4fb6fd8d084680d4b1d8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:08:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] l1-tokparse (report 66 items 7, 8): LLAMA_SERVER_TOK_CACHE on
 the SAFE_SPECIAL path (plain ranges: reuse only up to a boundary before the
 first byte where the range lists differ, occurrences inside a range are text;
 =2 compares with the full tokenization), LLAMA_SERVER_PARSE_INC=1 incremental
 stream parser (common_chat_parse_inc: input kept with the generation prompt,
 until() scans resumed through common_peg_parse_memo; =2 parses the old way
 too and logs MISMATCH, tqLLM update_reference pattern),
 LLAMA_SERVER_STREAM_STEP=1 one partial result per speculative step. All off
 by default. Tests: test-tok-cache (agent replay, 0 mismatches),
 test-chat-stream-inc (recorded outputs, oracle per update, per-step text and
 tool calls identical).

